          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Delhi HC to Rule on Whether Indian Government Bypassed Tender Process for National Emergency Alert System",
            "articleSection": "Policy & Rights",
            "abstract": "The Delhi High Court is set to rule on whether the Indian government bypassed a competitive tender process when awarding the contract for India's national emergency alert system to state-run CDOT, following a petition filed by Germany-based Utimaco. The case raises fundamental questions about procurement transparency and whether a monopoly arrangement for critical public safety infrastructure is legally defensible. An urgent hearing has been triggered, indicating the court views the matter as time-sensitive given the system's role in national emergency communications.",
            "url": "https://www.medianama.com/2026/05/223-delhi-hc-govt-bypassed-tender-process-india-emergency-alert-system/",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
              "url": "https://theaichronicle.com",
              "logo": {
